159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (An important part of the analytical process is preparing the data before performing detailed analysis. Datasets may contain missing entries, duplicate records, inconsistent formats, or incorrectly structured values that can affect the accuracy of subsequent results. Data cleaning and preparation therefore play a crucial role in ensuring that the information being analyzed is reliable. Once the data has been prepared, tools such as Microsoft Excel, Python with Pandas, and Power BI can be used to explore datasets, perform calculations, develop business measures, visualize trends, and communicate findings effectively.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (This report presents the work carried out during a six-week internship in the Data Analyst domain at BeeSkilled, with the practical activities documented across four major learning modules. The internship covered Excel-based sales analysis, Python and Pandas dataset exploration, Python-based data cleaning and wrangling, and an end-to-end business analytics and visualization capstone project. The overall experience provided an opportunity to apply concepts learned through the B.Tech CSE curriculum to practical data-analysis tasks and understand how raw datasets can be systematically processed and converted into meaningful, decision-oriented business insights.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
